# --help for every subcommand and nested verb (T60.2)

Top-level `rtok --help` stays in `help.toml`. `web` and `tui` are help-only
here: a server and a TTY are not snapshot material.

```console
$ rtok hook --help
Claude Code hook entry point: reads the event JSON on stdin, writes JSON to stdout

Usage: rtok hook [OPTIONS] <EVENT>

Arguments:
  <EVENT>  

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --host <HOST>    Overlay `[hook] host` (`claude` | `cursor` | `copilot`)
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok mcp --help
Serve MCP tools over stdio; `-- <server argv>` wraps a foreign server instead

Usage: rtok mcp [OPTIONS] [-- <WRAP>...]

Arguments:
  [WRAP]...  Foreign stdio MCP server to wrap losslessly (`rtok mcp -- npx some-server`)

Options:
      --call <TOOL>    Call one listed tool and print the text result (pi `registerTool` shim,
                       T70.3)
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --json <ARGS>    JSON arguments for `--call`
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok proxy --help
Local API proxy for ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL

Usage: rtok proxy [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>        User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --port <PORT>          Override `[proxy] port`
      --upstream <UPSTREAM>  Override `[proxy] upstream`
      --mode <MODE>          Override `[proxy] mode` (`passthrough` | `compress`)
      --dry-run              Print effective `[proxy]` settings and exit
  -h, --help                 Print help

$ rtok web --help
Local web UI over the same data as `rtok tui` (WebSocket API + Slint/WASM)

Usage: rtok web [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --host <HOST>    Override `[web] host`
      --port <PORT>    Override `[web] port`
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok tui --help
Terminal UI over the same data as `rtok web` (D23: one model, two renderings)

Usage: rtok tui [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>          User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --tab <TAB>              Start on this tab (a page name both surfaces carry)
      --tick-secs <TICK_SECS>  Model re-read cadence in seconds
  -h, --help                   Print help

$ rtok stats --help
Measurements from session logs and the proxy

Usage: rtok stats [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>         User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --since <SINCE>         How far back to read transcripts (`60d`, `24h`)
      --json                  JSON instead of the table
      --plugin <PLUGIN>       Restrict to one tool or plugin id
      --save-baseline <NAME>  Write this report JSON to `<home>/measurements/<name>.json`
      --compare <NAME>        Print deltas against a saved baseline
      --calibrate             Fit chars-per-token via count_tokens (skipped without an API key)
      --cache                 Cache health per session from proxy usage rows: busts and their cause
      --price                 Show per-model USD costs from `[stats.prices]` (`--price`)
  -h, --help                  Print help

$ rtok bench --help
A/B benchmark of host configurations

Usage: rtok bench [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>      User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --tasks <TASKS>      Task list TOML
      --runs <RUNS>        Repeats per task × config
      --dry-run            Print the schedule and exit
      --timeout <TIMEOUT>  Per-run timeout in seconds
      --suite <SUITE>      Task suite (`graph` = with/without rtok MCP)
  -h, --help               Print help

$ rtok doctor --help
Inspect hooks, MCP servers and the proxy chain

Usage: rtok doctor [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --instructions   Also run the instruction-file audit (T7.2)
      --json           JSON instead of the table
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok info --help
Version, effective paths, disk usage, error count and proxy status

Usage: rtok info [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --json           JSON instead of the text lines
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents --help
Agent hosts (`rtok agents install|uninstall|list|info …`)

Usage: rtok agents [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  install    Install hooks, MCP server and proxy into a host
  uninstall  Take rtok back out of a host: hooks, MCP entry, proxy variable, plugin link [alias:
             remove]
  list       Every known app: kind and name, path and version, config files, rtok modules
  info       One host: the same block `agents list` prints, just for that app
  sessions   What is running in this project: host, provider, model, tokens, start, run time
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents install --help
Install hooks, MCP server and proxy into a host

Usage: rtok agents install [OPTIONS] <HOST>

Arguments:
  <HOST>  Host(s), comma-separated (`claude`, `cursor`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `zcode`, `kimi`,
          `copilot`, `aider`, `windsurf`, `zed`, `vscode`)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --dry-run        Print the planned edits and exit
      --remove         Remove rtok from the host (hooks, MCP, proxy, plugin link); prefer `rtok
                       agents uninstall <host>`
      --mode <MODE>    Enable prompt modes (`terse,yagni`)
      --yes            Confirm destructive `--replace`
      --replace        Remove legacy token hooks and retarget the proxy
      --mcp            Register `rtok mcp` in the host MCP map
      --proxy          Set `env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` to this proxy
      --cli            Only the CLI app (`cursor`/`opencode` have CLI and desktop; default is all)
      --desktop        Only the desktop app (`cursor`/`opencode` have CLI and desktop; default is
                       all)
      --all            All variants (the default when neither `--cli` nor `--desktop` is given)
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents uninstall --help
Take rtok back out of a host: hooks, MCP entry, proxy variable, plugin link

Usage: rtok agents uninstall [OPTIONS] <HOST>

Arguments:
  <HOST>  Host(s), comma-separated (`claude`, `cursor`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `zcode`, `kimi`,
          `copilot`, `aider`, `windsurf`, `zed`, `vscode`)

Options:
      --config <PATH>  User config file (else `RTOK_CONFIG` or `<home>/config.toml`)
      --dry-run        Print what would be removed and exit
  -h, --help           Print help

$ rtok agents list --help
